course: dictionary
lesson: 8210
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Retreat can mean two different things, so context tells you which one to use. «After the army lost the battle, the soldiers began to retreat.» Here retreat means to move back or away, especially from danger or an enemy. Test it by putting "move back" into the sentence. It still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Retreat can also be a gentle word. «Jamie went to his room to retreat from the noise of the party.» Here it means to go somewhere quiet to rest or be alone. The words "from the noise" are the clue.
explain: Some words are used to hide how serious something is. «"Strategic withdrawal" is the official way to say an army retreated.» An official phrase can sound calmer than the plain truth. When you meet a fancy phrase like this, ask yourself what it really means, then check a dictionary if you are not sure.
fact: Retreat is a verb (retreat, retreats, retreated, retreating) and a noun (a retreat, retreats).
fact: «Retreat» means to move back or away, especially from danger or an enemy.
fact: «Retreat» can also mean a quiet place where you go to rest or be alone.
fact: «Strategic withdrawal» is the official way to say an army retreated.
fact: Phrases to know: beat a retreat, in full retreat, a weekend retreat.
exercise: «The Nationalist government retreated to Taiwan after the civil war.» What does retreated mean here? | *Moved back or away from danger | Made a loud speech to the crowd | Went shopping for new clothes | Stayed and fought at the front
exercise: Grandad says he needs a weekend retreat in the countryside. What is a retreat here? | A kind of train ticket | Fight with an enemy | *A quiet place to rest and be alone | Loud party with music all night
exercise: «"Strategic withdrawal" means a retreat.» What is the plain meaning of "strategic withdrawal"? | *An army moving back | A friendly visit to the enemy camp | A grand victory parade | A new kind of tent
test: «The waves began to retreat, leaving wet sand behind.» What does retreat mean here? | A quiet place to rest | Stay and fight | Grow bigger and higher | *Move back or away
test: Ella says, "I'll beat a retreat from this homework." What does beat a retreat mean? | Eat a big lunch | Ask a teacher for help | *Leave quickly, moving back | Start a race
exam: In «She went on a weekend retreat», what kind of word is retreat? | Verb | Adjective | *Noun | Adverb
